-- title:
--   Rational directions preserved by a Drinfeld chart isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime. For $i=1,2$ let $W_i$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\mathfrak m_{W_i}=(\pi_i)$ and with $q\in\mathfrak m_{W_i}$, and let $f_i,u_i,v_i\in W_i[[X_0,X_1]]$ (two-variable power series, indexed by `Fin 2`) be such that $u_i$ and $v_i$ are units and $f_i-(X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1)$ lies in $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$; write $S_i$ for the quotient of $W_i[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the principal ideal generated by $C(\pi_i)\,v_i-f_i\,u_i$. Let $\rho\colon W_1\to W_2$ be a ring homomorphism with $\rho(\pi_1)=\pi_2$, and let $\psi\colon S_1\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }S_2$ be a ring isomorphism with $\psi(\overline{C(w)})=\overline{C(\rho(w))}$ for every $w\in W_1$. Then there are power series $g_0,g_1\in W_2[[X_0,X_1]]$, each with vanishing constant coefficient, such that $\psi(\overline{X_i})=\overline{g_i}$ in $S_2$ for $i=0,1$, and such that the linear parts of $g_0,g_1$ carry rational directions to integral ones in the following sense: for all $a,b\in W_2$ with at least one of $a,b$ outside $\mathfrak m_{W_2}$ and with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_2}$, there exist a unit $\lambda\in W_2$ and natural numbers $n_0,n_1$ with $n_1<q$ and either $n_0=1$ or ($n_0=0$ and $n_1=1$), such that for $i=0,1$ the element $$\mathrm{coeff}_{X_0}(g_i)\,a+\mathrm{coeff}_{X_1}(g_i)\,b-\lambda\, n_i$$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_2}$.
--
--   This is the statement that an isomorphism between two Drinfeld local chart rings acts on the residual tangent plane by a matrix which permutes, up to scalars, the $\mathbb F_q$-rational directions, these being the projective zeros of the invariant form $X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1$ and hence representable by the integral vectors $(1,n)$ with $n<q$ together with $(0,1)$. It feeds the subsequent analysis of such isomorphisms in [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_apply_sub_C_eq_mk_of_ringEquiv_of_forall_apply_mk_C`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_apply_sub_C_eq_mk_of_ringEquiv_of_forall_apply_mk_C).
